# Start the line-in passthrough when the USB adapter actually appears
# (2026-09-12). A plain ConditionPathExists=/proc/asound/ICUSBAUDIO7D raced USB
# enumeration and lost: after a reboot the unit was skipped with "start
# condition unmet" and the passthrough was simply absent until started by hand.
#
# Device-activation is the fix — the sound device's own appearance is the event
# that makes the unit startable, so there is no window to lose.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="sound", KERNEL=="card*", ATTRS{idVendor}=="0d8c", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0102", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="wall-line-in.service"
